    {
      "title": "Start the Z-Assistant app and RetailZero API",
      "description": "## Start the Z-Assistant app and RetailZero API\n\nLet's start the Z-Assistant app and the RetailZero API. Z-Assistant will run on port 3000. Its tools call the RetailZero API which runs separately on port 3001.\n\n1. [Select this link](command:workbench.action.debug.start) to start both the Z-Assistant app and RetailZero API.\n1. Select **PORTS** tab at the bottom of this Codespace.\n1. Right-click on port **3000** and select **Port visibility** > **Public**.\n1. Repeat this step for port **3001**.\n\n\n### Check that everything launched successfully:\n\nIn the terminal, you should see two new terminal instances that have been added in the list to the right of the terminal: \n- Launch Z-Assistant\n- Launch RetailZero API\n\n#### If you select the **Launch Z-Assistant** tab, you should see something like:\n\n```\nDebugger attached.\nZ-Assistant running at http://localhost:3000\n```\n\n#### When you select the **Launch RetailZero API** tab, you should see something like:\n\n```\nDebugger attached.\nRetailZero API running at http://localhost:3001\n```",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 6,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 14,
          "character": 78
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Test Z-Assistant",
      "description": "## Test Z-Assistant\n\nNow let's verify that the Auth0 integration works.\n\n1. Select the **PORTS** tab. \n1. Hover over Port **3000** and select the globe icon that appear to open Z-Assistant in a new browser tab.\n3. **Sign up** for the application using a username and password you will be able to recall later.\n4. Ask Z-Assistant something simple: _\"What can you help me with?\"_\n    > You should get a response describing Z-Assistant's capabilities. Since we haven't added tools yet, it can only reply from its training knowledge, not from live RetailZero data.\n\n5. [Stop the application and API](command:workbench.action.debug.stop) when done.\n\nIn the next tour we will add the RetailZero tools.",
